---
title: Capture Records
sidebar:
  label: Capture records
  order: 4
---

`Capture Records` links a specimen to the collection event, site, coordinate,
method, and collector that produced it.

{% steps %}

1. Choose `Site ID` (only sites with collection events appear). The `Event ID`
   menu then filters to that site's collection events.
2. Choose `Event ID`.
3. Fill in the capture details below.

{% /steps %}

Changing `Site ID` or `Event ID` after one is set asks for confirmation, then
clears the linked event fields (`Method`, `Collector`, and `Coordinate ID`)
while keeping `Capture date` and `Capture time`. When you change only
`Event ID`, `Coordinate ID` is kept if it belongs to the same site.

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `Capture date`, `Capture time` | When the specimen was captured. |
| `Relative time` | Shown after `Show more` (or when enabled). Replaces exact `Capture time` with `Dawn`, `Morning`, `Afternoon`, `Dusk`, or `Night`. |
| `Method` | A collection method from the selected collection event. |
| `Method ID` | Optional trap, net, or other method identifier. Shown after `Show more`, or once it has a value. |
| `Coordinate ID` | A coordinate from the event's site. |
| `Coordinate extent (m)` | Optional positive distance (in meters) the capture extends beyond the coordinate point. |
| `Collector` | Optional, from the event's personnel. Shown when it has a value, after `Show more`, or always if `Always show collector field` is on in `Settings` > `Specimens`. |

In Darwin Core exports, a positive `Coordinate extent (m)` value is added to
the coordinate's saved uncertainty (`coordinateUncertaintyInMeters`). If the
coordinate has no valid uncertainty, the extent is used by itself. Empty, zero,
and negative values are ignored.
